  <h2>Military-Friendly Communities in North San Antonio</h2>

  <p>North San Antonio is the epicenter of military family living in Texas. With close proximity to Fort Sam Houston and excellent schools, several communities have become military favorites. Let's explore the best options.</p>

  <h3>Schertz: Growing Family Haven</h3>
  <p>Schertz is experiencing explosive growth with new construction, excellent schools, and strong military presence. Perfect for military families seeking modern homes and family-friendly amenities.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Population: ~35,000 and growing</li>
    <li>Schools: Schertz-Cibolo-Universal City ISD (highly rated)</li>
    <li>Military Presence: Strong</li>
    <li>Homes: Mix of new construction and resale</li>
    <li>BAH Friendly: Excellent value</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cibolo: New Construction Capital</h3>
  <p>Cibolo is known for its abundance of new construction homes. Builders are constantly developing new communities, making it ideal for military families wanting modern, warranty-backed homes.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Population: ~35,000</li>
    <li>New Construction: Abundant</li>
    <li>Schools: Top-rated</li>
    <li>Amenities: Growing rapidly</li>
    <li>Community Feel: Family-oriented</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Universal City: Convenient North Location</h3>
  <p>Small but convenient community on the North Side with excellent schools and strong military culture. Great for families wanting established neighborhoods with easy commutes.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Population: ~19,000</li>
    <li>Schools: Schertz-Cibolo-Universal City ISD</li>
    <li>Commute: Short to bases</li>
    <li>Community: Tight-knit</li>
    <li>Affordability: Good</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Converse: Affordable Military Favorite</h3>
  <p>Converse offers affordable housing perfect for military budgets. Strong military presence, good schools, and welcoming community make it popular with PCS families.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Population: ~25,000</li>
    <li>Affordability: Excellent</li>
    <li>Military Presence: Very strong</li>
    <li>Schools: Quality education</li>
    <li>Growth: Steady</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Choosing Your North San Antonio Community</h2>
  <p>Consider your family's priorities: new homes, established neighborhoods, school ratings, commute times, and budget. I can help match your family with the perfect community.</p>
